compbench (2.3-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Fix read benchmark measuring cached data instead of disk: drop
    page cache before the cold read test.
  * Add zlib compression algorithm alongside zstd and lzo.
  * Report write/read throughput standard deviation in CSV (WrStddev,
    RdStddev) for repeated runs.
  * Harden integer parsing (--repeat, --hdd, --zstd) with strtol
    validation instead of atoi.
  * Fix ETA accuracy by counting every attempted test as progress.
  * Add manual page (compbench.1).
  * Add "make uninstall" target.
  * CSV metadata: human-readable force mode, renamed duplicate
    "Archive" label, add Host/Kernel/Date for reproducibility.
  * Refactor test loop to eliminate duplication; unify disk-stat
    readers; poll for partition nodes instead of a fixed sleep.
  * Move large result arrays off the stack.

 -- Robin DUBREUIL <robin@dubreuil.pro>  Sun, 14 Jun 2026 12:00:00 +0000

compbench (2.2-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Fix zstd level range to match Btrfs: -15..15 (was incorrectly 1-19).
  * Support negative zstd levels (-15..-1), available since kernel 6.15.

